cookbook/decisions/restart-the-port-from-isaiahs-clean-base.md:130:Isaiah's critical pins are unchanged: torch 2.9.0, triton 3.5.0, flash-attn 2.8.3, numpy, pydantic, wandb, mypy. The other 55 changed dependency names (plus the `owl` requirement record) are kaggle-environments' own dependency tree (e.g. jax 0.10 → 0.11.2; `click` is shared with W&B, whose live telemetry was not exercised). Checks with 1.32.7: `just prepare` passes, with Rust 155 passed / 2 ignored (expensive action-angle audits; Orbit replay and generation parity pass) and Python 722 passed / 3 skipped. Codex independently reproduced the lock byte-for-byte from the recorded `uv remove` + `uv add` (`ops/deps-independent-verification-fb65e1f/`).
cookbook/decisions/recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah-without-owner-escalation.md:41:This record changes no training config and starts no run. The historical 4,096/spm 1/accumulation 2 cadence with teachers disabled lives only on the reference branch. After the [[restart-the-port-from-isaiahs-clean-base|restart]], the rebuilt configs must adopt these targets from the start, and alignment is complete only after GPU qualification. Rebuild Task 3.4 encodes target 1 in `configs/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml` and `configs/kaggriculture_4rank.yaml` ([[../references/kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe|configs Reference]]). At `kg/rebuild-configs` `99e5124`, independent verification (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-3.4-r3/report.md`) found that all three Kaggriculture YAMLs load through `FullConfig` with the Task 3.1 model registration, the factory constructs their models (meta-device loader probe), and `scripts/run_ppo.py` checks every forward workload against the model's GEMM chunking at startup through the real loader. Its CPU checks: `pytest tests/kaggriculture tests/owl tests/scripts tests/tools -m 'not slow'` 1,373 passed, 4 skipped (none of them config-integration cases); `mypy python/owl scripts` no issues in 59 files; `cargo test --locked --offline` 155 passed, 2 ignored; removing the startup `_check_model_workload` call took the four startup cases from 4 passed to 4 failed and back to 4 passed on restoration. These checks cover config semantics and startup checking only. `run_ppo` still stops explicitly after the workload check because native environment and trainer integration are pending; teacher and replay execution, dense-state memory, real Inductor/FlashAttention compilation, GPU throughput and competitive strength remain unqualified, and no training or GPU run has been performed.
cookbook/decisions/diagnose-the-mechanism-before-spending-on-runs.md:22:V3 operationalizes those requirements as follows. Before a costly run, state the observed problem, code/data path, supported mechanism or diagnostic question, expected discriminating observation, and stopping condition. Preserve source/configuration, inputs, seeds and outputs sufficient to replay and localize it. Inspect implementation or add focused diagnostics when visibility is missing. A diagnostic may resolve an unknown cause; mark uncertainty rather than inventing confidence.
cookbook/decisions/index.md:3:- [[restart-the-port-from-isaiahs-clean-base|Restart the port from Isaiah's clean base]] — Restart from Isaiah's 32b3ec9 with reviewed reference reuse and the same layer topology; BC and RTX PRO 6000 verification follow. Task 1.1 rebuilds a standalone hash-pinned kernel: 59 engine tests, four replays/2,876 transitions, green preparation (769 Python cases), isolated Cargo checks and explicit vendored-style exceptions; checker hardened after verification round 1. Task 1.1 feature isolation is historical; Task 1.3 adds the root consumer with L4 repair.

